From 1283e63365d036481e384ccb7aece4afca213d94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GallopLin <1317864235@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:10:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] feat(bench): single-GPU INT8 moments, ablation switches,
 LR-scheduler fix, step timing in all trainers

- trainer_multistream: PCCHECK_MS_QUANT=1 restores the single-GPU int8
  moment path (lost in the merge tree); scheduler and grad-scaler state are
  attached to the extra blob
- LR scheduler is now stepped on checkpoint steps, before finalize, so the
  captured state matches the update (it used to be skipped, so the LR
  schedule drifted with cf)
- ablation switches: PCCHECK_MS_SCHEDULE=progressive|after_step and
  PCCHECK_MS_WAR=group|global
- StepTimer in trainer_{multistream,pccheck,checkfreq,gpm}; CheckFreq/GPM
  warmup now from PCCHECK_BENCH_WARMUP like the others
- trainer_pccheck drains the tail checkpoint before stopping the monitor

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
